COMMAND NAME: gpmigrator

Upgrades an existing Greenplum Database 3.1.x.x system to 3.2.


*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

gpmigrator <old_GPHOME_path> <new_GPHOME_path> 
           [-d <master_data_directory>] [-l <logfile_directory>] [-q]

gpmigrator --prepare 
          [ --noinit | 
            --master_port <port> --port_base <port> --mirror_port_base <port> ] 
          <old_GPHOME_path> <new_GPHOME_path> 
          [-d <master_data_directory>] [-l <logfile_directory>] [-q]

gpmigrator --version | --help


*****************************************************
PREREQUISITES
*****************************************************

The following tasks should be performed prior to executing an upgrade:

* Make sure you are logged in to the master host as the Greenplum 
  Database superuser (gpadmin).

* Install the Greenplum Database 3.2.0.x binaries on all Greenplum hosts.

* Copy any custom modules from your 3.1 installation to your 3.2 
  installation on all Greenplum hosts. For example, shared library 
  files for user-defined functions in $GPHOME/lib or PostgreSQL add-on 
  modules (such as plr.so or pgcrypto.so) in $GPHOME/lib/postgresql.

* Check for and recover any failed segments in your current Greenplum 
  Database system (gpstate, gprecoverseg).

* Verify the integrity of your 3.1.x.x system catalogs using the 
  --prepare step of gpmigrator. This will check your system catalogs 
  and indexes. By default, it will also initialize a temporary 3.2 system 
  that you can use to verify your segment configuration prior to executing 
  the upgrade (use --noinit to skip this step). If problems are found, 
  contact Greenplum customer support.

* Backup your 3.1.x.x databases (gpcrondump or ZFS snapshots).

* Remove the standby master from your system configuration 
  (gpinitstandby -r).

* Do a clean shutdown of your 3.1.x.x system (gpstop).

* Update your environment to point to the new 3.2 installation.

* Inform all database users of the upgrade and lockout time frame. 
  Once the upgrade is in process, users will not be allowed on the 
  system until the upgrade is complete.


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The gpmigrator utility upgrades an existing Greenplum Database 3.1.x.x 
system to 3.2. It can also be used to downgrade a 3.2 system back to 3.1. 
This utility updates the system catalog and internal version number, but 
not the actual software binaries.

During the migration process, all client connections to the master will 
be locked out. The migration utility locks all client access to the master, 
however it does not block direct utility mode access to the segments. 
To ensure a safe upgrade, make sure users are aware that any connections 
to a Greenplum segment are not safe during the upgrade time frame.

Prior to executing the upgrade, you can optionally run gpmigrator in 
prepare mode to perform some pre-upgrade validation without actually 
executing the upgrade. The prepare phase does three things; it runs a 
utility called gpcheckcat to verify your system catalogs, it checks 
for invalid indexes that need rebuilding, and it initializes a temporary 
3.2 system from which you can validate your segment configuration. You 
can optionally skip the initialization step by specifying --noinit.


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

<old_GPHOME_path>

Required. The absolute path to the current version of Greenplum 
Database software you want to migrate away from.


<new_GPHOME_path>

Required. The absolute path to the new version of Greenplum Database 
software you want to migrate to.


--prepare

Optional. Running gpmigrator with the --prepare option will perform 
some pre-upgrade validation, but not execute the upgrade. The prepare 
phase does three things; it runs a utility called gpcheckcat to verify 
your system catalogs, it checks for invalid indexes that need rebuilding, 
and it initializes a temporary 3.2 system from which you can validate 
your segment configuration (use --noinit to skip this step). 


--master_port <port>
--port_base <port>
--mirror_port_base <port>

Used with the --prepare option to supply a temporary master port, 
primary segment port base, and mirror segment port base for the 
temporary 3.2 system to be initialized. These must be different that 
what your current 3.1.x.x system is using. If not supplied on the 
command-line, then gpmigrator will prompt you for them.


--noinit

When used with the --prepare option, will skip the initialization 
step. The prepare phase will verify system catalogs and check for 
invalid indexes, but not initialize a temporary 3.2 system. 


-d master_data_directory

Optional. The current master host data directory. If not specified, 
the value set for $MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.


-l logfile_directory

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/gpAdminLogs.


-q (quiet mode)

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, 
but is still written to the log file.


--help

Displays the online help.


--version

Displays the version of this utility. 


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Perform pre-upgrade validation (skipping the initialization step), 
but do not execute the upgrade:

/usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.4/bin/gpmigrator --prepare --noinit \
/usr/local/greenplum-db-3.1.1.9 \
/usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.4


Upgrade to version 3.2 from version 3.1.1.9 (first make sure you 
are using the 3.2 version of the Greenplum utilities):

source /usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.4/greenplum_path.sh

gpmigrator /usr/local/greenplum-db-3.1.1.9 
/usr/local/greenplum-db-3.2.0.4


